{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Blue & Lonesome feels like a natural next choice because its blues focus connects directly with what interests me in Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "Best of The Animals shares that blues-influenced rock appeal, while CSNY 1974 and Carole King Tapestry connect with my interest in classic rock and songwriting."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "24K Magic's contemporary pop and funk direction does not fit the blues and guitar music I want on this visit, even though I can enjoy soulful music.",
    "Django and Jimmie's traditional country duet focus is not what I am seeking today, and Big City gives me too little information to make a confident connection."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in classic artists as a reason to offer almost any familiar older act, when the particular sound matters more to me today.",
    "Several hits collections assume I want familiar favorites, but recognizing an artist does not give me a strong reason to choose another collection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The blues and guitar connection in Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters more to my choice today than a broad connection to classic rock or soul.",
    "I rarely choose much at once: several albums can appeal to me, but only Blue & Lonesome feels compelling enough for me to act on during this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in classic rock and soul, but only a few capture the blues and guitar focus driving my choice today."
}"}
